Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: visionox-vtdr6130-cog: add the AYN Odin 3 Portal

The Odin 3 Portal's 7" 1080x1920 AMOLED is a VTDR6130 (compatible
"vtdr6130,o3p"), 60/120 Hz picked with command 0x6c, DSC 12-line slices.

Armada's three patches (armada-os/armada main, packages/kernel/patches),
squashed onto our driver:
 - 1111 (Pocket Duo panel): per-panel ordered supplies with voltages and
   loads, vendor writes as DCS long packets, display-off delay and default
   brightness from the descriptor. The RP5/RP6/Flip 2 descriptors set none
   of these, so their sequences are unchanged; the Duo's compatible comes
   along and is unused here.
 - 1304: the Odin 3 Portal's modes, init sequence and supplies (vddio,
   tvdd), its display-off kept in LPM.
 - 1305: frame_len_120/frame_len_60 on the DSI device to calibrate the
   DDIC frame lengths per unit.
Not taken: Armada 0049 (the DPU's opt-in 8 bpc dither), which the
Odin 3 Portal dts asks for with armada,dpu-8bpc-dither.

